## 1. Why this document exists

Org hygiene records cross-repo product identity: pure .oo + C + seed, zero .rs scans, rename of no-Rust branding to product language, and honest bash residual (chicken-egg).

## 2. Problem statement

Multi-repo orgs drift: docs, QA, and site tell different purity stories.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- Multi-repo governance docs.
- Brand/product language guides.
- Build-input purity analogies (supply-chain hygiene).

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

RS_COUNT=0 table; shell residual list; rename map (ci_product, product.yml).

## 5. Limits and failure modes

May be monorepo-local only. Must not replace ooda residual docs.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

Used for 2026-08 hygiene pass; ensure committed where the org can see it.

## 8. Open questions

1. Publish under .github org profile?
2. Org-wide zero-.rs CI scan?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Site/product language matches renames.
- [ ] Shell residual list stays honest.

